    fullDescription: "The Sidemen Valley in eastern Bali is one of the island's most beautiful and peaceful escapes — a lush landscape of unspoilt rice terraces, small traditional villages and an ever-present view of the towering Mount Agung volcano, all about 1.5 hours from Ubud. Often described as 'the Bali of 20 years ago', Sidemen has been spared the mass tourism of the south and Ubud, retaining a genuinely rural, unhurried character: farmers work the terraced paddies by hand, weavers craft traditional songket textiles threaded with gold, and the pace of life is slow and authentic. A day here is about soaking up the scenery and village life rather than ticking off attractions — walking or scootering the terraced lanes, visiting a weaving workshop, sampling local coffee and cacao, and drinking in those volcano views. It pairs beautifully with the nearby Tirta Gangga water palace, with its ornamental pools and stepping stones, just 30 minutes away. While doable as a full-day trip with a driver (around $40), Sidemen truly rewards an overnight at one of its lovely eco-resorts, letting you catch the rice terraces glowing in the dawn light. For serene, authentic, crowd-free Bali, Sidemen is a treasure.",
